DESCRIPTION:National Young Readers Day is an American reading observance ma
 rked in November\, and a useful example of how thin the documentation behi
 nd a widely listed day can be. The Library of Congress published mentions 
 of it in 1993 and 1995\, the second describing Pizza Hut — the company b
 ehind the BOOK IT! classroom reading program — as cosponsor alongside th
 e Library's own Center for the Book. What no primary source we could find 
 states is who created the day\, in what year\, or by what date rule.\n\nht
